+# RQ-0128 — Prepayments, deposits and the single-supply path (T-0047)
+
+## Question
+
+- **Q1.** The accounting questions of the card (postings.md Q7, Q10; the `gst_supply_pattern`
+  decision) — are any still open?
+- **Q2.** ADR-0045 R2 adds the system role `GST_ATTRIBUTED_UNBILLED` to "the SQL role CHECK of
+  `app.account_system_role` (additive migration that widens the list)". Can that CHECK be widened
+  forward-only?
+- **Q3.** ADR-0045 R6 leaves one choice to T-0047: how the G1 amount of a `GST-UB` line is carried —
+  `tax_grossed` (tax × (1 + rate) / rate) on the BAS map, or a new nullable
+  `journal_line.tax_base_amount`. Which one, and can either be stored forward-only?
+- **Q4.** Where do the classification (R1), the prepayment receipt, the deposit invoice and the
+  application on the final invoice live, given the ledger rules (documents outside `packages/ledger`,
+  posted = immutable, CUSTOMER_PREPAYMENTS is not a control account)?
+- **Q5.** What of R9 can be built now without new golden postings?
+
+## Sources
+
+| # | Source | Accessed | Kind | What it says |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | RQ-0095 Q7, Q10; `Docs/accounting/postings.md` GP-012…GP-015, GP-012-B, GP-015-B (Approved) | 2026-11-09 | record / golden | Option B at receipt; deposit invoice credits CUSTOMER_PREPAYMENTS; the final invoice nets the prepayment in one journal; single-supply variants. Q7/Q10 answered 2026-11-08. |
+| S2 | ADR-0045 (Accepted 2026-11-09, DL-0387), persona re-review `.agent/evidence/T-0124/accounting-rereview-20261109.md` (M3) | 2026-11-09 | ADR / review | R1–R9; R6 needs G1 = 7,700.00 for the 700.00 GST-UB line of GP-012-B; the carrier is open. |
+| S3 | `packages/db/src/migrate.ts` (policy RULES), migration 0005 (inline `role IN (...)` CHECK, `app.system_role_allows`, `account_guard_bound`), 0036 header and DL-0257/RQ-0102 finding 6 (the `subkind` precedent) | 2026-11-09 | code / record | The runner refuses any `DROP CONSTRAINT`; an inline CHECK cannot be replaced. 0036 refined `tax_code.kind` with an additive `subkind` column instead. `CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION` that keeps the contract is allowed (migration skill). |
+| S4 | PostgreSQL 16/17 manual, `ALTER TABLE` (prior knowledge; postgresql.org reachable in earlier sessions, RQ-0016) | 2026-11-09 | primary (prior knowledge) | A CHECK constraint's expression cannot be altered; only `DROP CONSTRAINT` + `ADD CONSTRAINT`. `CREATE VIEW ... WITH (security_invoker = true)` (PG ≥ 15) runs the view's table access with the caller's rights, so RLS of the base tables applies. |
+| S5 | `packages/ledger/src/hash-chain.ts`, RQ-0016 canonical form `lf-journal-v1` | 2026-11-09 | code / record | The hash covers a fixed list of `journal_line` columns. A new column would not be covered by v1, so its value could change undetected (posted rows are immutable by trigger, but the chain is the tamper evidence). Covering it needs a canonical v2 for every company. |
+| S6 | `packages/modules/tax/src/bas-compute.ts`, migration 0036 (`bas_label_map.amount` inline CHECK `gross|net|tax`) | 2026-11-09 | code | The map's `amount` cannot be widened in place either; a refining column following the `subkind` pattern can. |
+| S7 | `packages/modules/ar/src/sales-invoices.ts`, `receipts.ts`, `invoice-journal.ts`, migrations 0037, 0039 | 2026-11-09 | code | Invoice journal = AR, ROUNDING, revenue per (account, code), GST per code; receipts refuse `NO_ALLOCATION` and point to T-0047. Source types `ar.prepayment` and `ar.prepayment_application` exist in the period matrix and the cash-basis table (`immediate` / `settlement`). |
+
+## Findings
+
+1. **Q1 — nothing open.** Q7/Q10 are answered (S1) and ADR-0045 is Accepted (S2). The only open
+   accounting choice is Q3, which ADR-0045 delegates to T-0047.
+2. **Q2 — the CHECK cannot be widened; bind new roles in an additive table.** Following the 0036
+   precedent (S3), migration 0045 adds `app.account_system_role_ext` (tenant table, RLS ENABLE +
+   FORCE, same binding trigger as 0005) whose role CHECK calls a new IMMUTABLE function
+   `app.system_role_is_extended(role)` (today: `GST_ATTRIBUTED_UNBILLED`). A later role extends the
+   function with `CREATE OR REPLACE`, never a new table. `app.system_role_allows` is replaced with the
+   same contract plus `GST_ATTRIBUTED_UNBILLED → asset`; `app.account_guard_bound` is replaced to check
+   both binding tables. A `security_invoker` view `app.system_role_binding` (UNION ALL of both) is
+   what role resolution reads: the posting engine, the BAS line reader and the golden world.
+3. **Q3 — `tax_grossed`.** `journal_line.tax_base_amount` would sit outside the `lf-journal-v1`
+   hash (S5) unless every company's chain moved to a v2 canonical form — a ledger-wide change for one
+   BAS label. `tax_grossed` changes no ledger table: migration 0045 adds
+   `bas_label_map.amount_rule` (`tax_grossed` only; requires `amount = 'tax'`; fixed after insert),
+   and the BAS computes G1 = tax × (1 + rate) / rate, half-up to cents, with the rate of the tax-code
+   version on the line's date. Trade-off: the base is derived from a rounded tax, so for a base whose
+   GST rounds, G1 can differ from base + tax by at most 0.005 × 11 = 0.055 (10 % rate) — under one
+   cent per 0.01 of rounding on a label lodged in whole dollars. GP-012-B: 700.00 × 11 = 7,700.00
+   exactly. Recorded in DL-0390 and in an appended note to ADR-0045.
+4. **Q4 — documents in `packages/modules/ar`, ledger writes through `post()`.**
+   - Prepayment receipt: new document table `app.ar_prepayment` (immutable after insert), posted as
+     source type `ar_prepayment`. CUSTOMER_PREPAYMENTS is not a control account, so there is no
+     subledger item; "unapplied" is derived from the application table.
+   - Deposit invoice: a sales invoice with `billing_format = 'deposit'`; its lines credit
+     CUSTOMER_PREPAYMENTS (GP-014, Q10) instead of the profile's revenue account. Tax comes from the
+     same GST calculation.
+   - Classification (R1): `gst_supply_pattern` + `gst_supply_pattern_confirmed_by/_at` on both
+     documents, CHECKed, no default; on `sales_invoice` required when `billing_format = 'deposit'`.
+     `single_supply` also stores `supply_net_total` (R9(a)).
+   - Application: `app.ar_deposit_application` rows (final invoice → prepayment or deposit invoice),
+     written with the draft, each source applicable once (unique). The final invoice's journal gets
+     Dr CUSTOMER_PREPAYMENTS after the AR line, AR and GST collected reduced (GP-013/GP-015); for
+     `single_supply` the GP-015-B shape (no tax codes, GST_ATTRIBUTED_UNBILLED credited).
+   - Engine guard (R6): `GST-UB` only on the account bound to `GST_ATTRIBUTED_UNBILLED`, and no other
+     tax code on that account (`ATTRIBUTION_TAX_CODE`).
+5. **Q5 — R9(a) and R9(d) now; R9(b) and (c) need golden Drafts.** R9(a) is a refusal and R9(d) a
+   read-only listing. R9(b) (price variation) and R9(c) (cancellation) post journals whose golden
+   Drafts "are written by T-0047 before build"; this build may not edit `postings.md` (lead
+   instruction) and a Draft cannot be built before it is Approved, so both move to follow-up card
+   **T-0170**, and until then a final invoice whose GST differs from the GST attributed is refused
+   (`SINGLE_SUPPLY_VARIATION`) — never posted with a guessed adjustment.
+
+## Conclusion
+
+Build per findings 2–5; DL-0390 (G1 carrier), DL-0391 (role binding table), DL-0392 (documents and
+application), DL-0393 (scope split T-0170/T-0171).
